# AI / adaptive sensing

- Multi-stage: quality → features → baseline → cross-modal confidence → event → spatial → explanation. Not one ML model.
- Sensor quality ≠ event confidence. Severity ≠ confidence. Environment vs fault vs uncertain.
- PMS/SCD41 quantitative; BME688/MQ135 are features — never fake ppm.
- V1 engines first (quality, baseline, cross-modal C, rule policy, basic anomaly, classifier, basic spatial, explanations). ML only if it beats simple baselines.
- VoI/energy is a hypothesis. Do not claim energy savings without evidence (C-19).
- Node: deterministic policy. Gateway: heavy ML. No TFLite/TinyML (ADR-001, ADR-017).
- Evidence traces always. SHAP required when a tree/boosting model is deployed; not on rule engines.
- AI failure → deterministic fallback; never drop the observation.

This rule does not override SAD SHAP wording until that document is revised; implement traces always and SHAP when models exist.
